A||N||7||88formula||Need information on custom pistons for 3.4-liter engine.||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||04-20-2001||04:14 PM||||If anyone has had custom pistons made for a 3.4-liter Camaro engine before than I need to know what you got. I am considering this option since the only pistons available for this engine that are stronger than stock are the crappy Federal Mogul DOHC pistons. I read somewhere before that someone had custom pistons from Ross pistons but I cannot remember who it was. <P>Thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Dave Gunsul||04-20-2001||08:17 PM||||I'm getting custom Ross pistons for my 3.2.<BR>Any performance machine shop should be able to get them for you. They'll just need the bore size and head cc size.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||04-20-2001||09:50 PM||||You can also send out an old piston and they will copy it for you. I was hoping to get some information from someone who has already done the legwork. <P>What are the pistons costing you?<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||owenslee||04-22-2001||12:23 PM||||88Formula...<P>Although they are not forged pistons, Federal Mogul DOES sell a hypereutectic piston for the 3.4 Camaro that is NOT the 3.4 DOHC piston.<P>The part number is H800P and compression ratio is 9.2-9.5 depending on overbore and any head / block surfacing.<P>These are the same pistons used the in remanufactured 3.4 engines from Grooms that Ed parks is using and recommending.<P>Do a search for an earlier post I left for 3.4 pistons. In that post I include ring dimensions and part numbers as well.<P>Hope that helps.<P>Kerry||||reg||14
Z||000004||Dave Gunsul||04-22-2001||12:51 PM||||My custom Ross pistons are costing me $91 a <BR>piece!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> But at 10:1 comp. I'll pay it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Note: this is for a 3.1<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||04-22-2001||02:23 PM||||Dave,<P>Did you have a machine shop measure and order the pistons for you or did you do that yourself? How much do the pistons weigh with the wrist pin? The stock pistons weigh 536 grams for a 3.4-liter motor (3.620 bore). Help me out here???<P><BR>Thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dave Gunsul||04-22-2001||08:28 PM||||unfortunately, I don't have an answer for some of your questions right now because the<BR>machine shop has just started on the block.<BR>I bought the Fiero stores perf. heads and took one over to the machine shop on thursday<BR>for them to measure for the pistons.<BR>They tell me that the pistons will take 2 <BR>weeks!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> So I won't know anything about the<BR>weight and other specs until then. <BR>Guess we'll both be waiting in excitment for<BR>my engine. ;-)<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||04-22-2001||08:37 PM||||That’s OK chances are I'll have the machine shop order me a set if I can't find what I want. <P>Thanks anyway.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
